<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka two-year bond yields at 12.78 percent.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka two-year bond yields at 12.78 percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's Central Bank said the the latest auction for two-year Treasury Bonds on Friday was heavily oversubscribed and successful bidders were allocated bonds at a weighted average yield of 12.78 percent.</p>
<p>	 Amount offered:	  500 million rupees</p>
<p>	 Bids received:	 1.225 billion rupees</p>
<p>	 Amount accepted:	 500 million rupees</p>
<p>	 Weighted avg yield:  12.78 percent per year (current)</p>
<p>				    12.75 percent (previous)</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
